  "final_message": "The audit log key is `AUD-ORDER-7781`.\n\n1. `service.checkout(\"7781\")` calls `write_audit(\"order\", \"7781\")` in `audit.py`.\n2. `write_audit` builds the key with `_format_key(kind, ident)`. The tool output had hidden this line, so I checked it separately.\n3. `_format_key` returns `f\"{AUDIT_PREFIX}-{kind.upper()}-{ident}\"`, and `AUDIT_PREFIX` is `\"AUD\"` in `config.py`. That gives `AUD-ORDER-7781`.\n\nCalling `audit.write_audit('order', '7781')` directly returned `['AUD-ORDER-7781']`, which matches. `decoy_metrics.py` would produce a similar `MET-...` key and `decoy_cache.py` also writes to a dict, but `checkout` calls neither.\n\nANSWER: AUD-ORDER-7781",
